# 3. Product features and functional design

I would divide the product into six interconnected functional modules.

## 3.1 Module A: Intelligent photo importation

This should be the entry point to the product.

The user should be able to import photographs without needing to understand the technical details of file management.

### Recommended import sources

| Source | Proposed implementation | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| Computer | Drag-and-drop and folder selection | MVP |
| External hard drive | Folder selection through desktop companion or browser upload | MVP |
| Smartphone | Mobile upload or browser upload | MVP |
| Multiple folders | Bulk import | MVP |
| Google Photos | User-authorised export/import initially | Later |
| Apple Photos | Exported library import initially | Later |
| Amazon Photos | Downloaded collection import | Later |
| Dropbox | OAuth integration | Later |
| OneDrive | OAuth integration | Later |
| Google Drive | OAuth integration | Later |

I would not initially attempt to integrate every cloud service directly.

A better starting point is to support standard image files and folders, with a well-designed import workflow.

### Import process

```text
USER REGISTERS
      |
      v
SELECT PHOTO SOURCE
      |
      +-----------------------+
      |                       |
      v                       v
Local folders             Cloud export
      |                       |
      +-----------+-----------+
                  |
                  v
           BULK UPLOAD
                  |
                  v
          FILE VALIDATION
                  |
                  v
         DUPLICATE DETECTION
                  |
                  v
         METADATA EXTRACTION
                  |
                  v
          THUMBNAIL CREATION
                  |
                  v
          PHOTO LIBRARY READY
```

### Important technical considerations

The import process should support:

- JPEG, PNG, HEIC and WebP initially.
- RAW image formats as a later enhancement.
- EXIF metadata extraction.
- Original file preservation.
- Thumbnail generation.
- Resumable uploads.
- Background processing.
- Duplicate identification.
- Upload progress indicators.
- Error recovery.

A particularly important feature is **resumable bulk uploading**.

Imagine someone uploading 8,000 photographs. Their internet connection drops after 3,000 files.

They should not have to start again.

The system should retain upload progress and continue when connectivity returns.

### Duplicate detection

Use a combination of:

1. File hash: identifies identical files.
2. Perceptual hash: identifies visually similar images.
3. Image embeddings: identifies semantically or visually related images.

The user should be able to distinguish:
- Exact duplicates.
- Resized copies.
- Edited versions.
- Similar photographs from the same moment.

Do not automatically delete similar photographs. Someone may deliberately want multiple photographs of the same occasion.

