## 21. What I would do next: Move from concept to product design

I recommend treating the next phase as a proper product-development exercise, with five deliverables.

| Deliverable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| 1. Product Requirements Document (PRD) | Define exactly what the product must do |
| 2. UX/UI prototype | Design the actual user experience and application screens |
| 3. Technical architecture specification | Define the backend, database, AI and storage implementation |
| 4. MVP development specification | Break functionality into implementable modules and development tasks |
| 5. Commercial validation plan | Test demand, pricing and willingness to pay |

**One final strategic suggestion:** Before commissioning development, build an interactive prototype of the main user journey. Demonstrate registration, bulk upload, an automatically organised timeline, suggested albums, AI captions and memory discovery using sample photographs.

This will allow potential customers to experience the proposition before substantial development expenditure.

The ultimate test is not whether the AI can describe photographs. It is whether someone can upload years of disorganised photographs, see their memories come together and genuinely feel that the product has given them something valuable they did not previously have.

**That is the product worth building.**